A||N||1||yellow_fiero||OIL PAN removal on an '88 V6 help...||||11||
Z||000000||yellow_fiero||04-21-2000||11:21 AM||||My oil pan has rusted through and needs repair.  I have searched the wonderful threads and I have realized that this has been hashed out a few times, on a few good threads.  However, all the threads I saw were about how to replace the pan on pre-88 V6s.  I'm assuming that the '88 Formula chassis is different than the rest of the years.  Has anyone attempted changing the oil pan on an '88 Fiero?  I don't have an engine hoist, but I do have a jack and some jack stands.  Also, the Hayes manual is not to be believed right?  Thanks so much in advance.||||reg||11
Z||000001||Gokart||04-21-2000||09:34 PM||||Not sure what the details are for 88, but did notice the reply you got on Fiero egroups. Maybe the 2x4 worked for your advisor, but it's not necessary. Just a bottle jack placed the right way raising the alternator bracket was enough for me to remove the engine mount required to get the oil pan out.<p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 04-21-2000).]||||reg||1
